{"identifier":"babies_and_breadwinners_2","title":"Babies and Breadwinners (Part II)","description":"Presented by: U.S. Department of Health, Education and Welfare, Public Health Service and Bureau State Services. Produced by the Communicable Disease Center in cooperation with the Georgia Department of Public Health and the Muscogee Health","videoUrl":"https://archive.org/download/babies_and_breadwinners_2/babies_and_breadwinners_2_512kb.mp4","thumbnailUrl":"https://archive.org/services/img/babies_and_breadwinners_2","sourcePageUrl":"https://archive.org/details/babies_and_breadwinners_2","durationMs":595001,"level":"C1","topic":"Motion Pictures: Government;Health and Hygiene;Medicine: Infectious Diseases","sourceCredit":"Source: Internet Archive — Babies and Breadwinners (Part II)","hasCaptions":true,"segments":[{"startMs":1,"endMs":7000,"text":"Before the immunization stations opened, the junior team of commerce began a house-to-house canvas."},{"startMs":9001,"endMs":13001,"text":"Good afternoon. Hello. I'm Bill Jones from the Columbus Junior Chamber of Commerce."},{"startMs":14000,"endMs":21001,"text":"We're in the neighborhood advertising this polio vaccine station is set up up at Hershey's grocery this afternoon. They'll be up there at seven o'clock to give"},{"startMs":21001,"endMs":24000,"text":"free polio shots to you and any members of your family."},{"startMs":27000,"endMs":34001,"text":"I'm Robert George with the Columbus Junior Chamber of Commerce. It's going to be a free polio station set up here in your community that ran the chicken shack. We"},{"startMs":34001,"endMs":46001,"text":"would like for you and your family to come down. The chief of police endorsed the program and cooperated in many practical ways. They're going to have traffic"},{"startMs":46001,"endMs":56000,"text":"problems. You're in a traffic division, I want you to assist them wherever way you possibly can. And anything you can do for them. I want you to go all out."},{"startMs":58000,"endMs":63000,"text":"And tomorrow at 12th Street and Broadway, they're going to have a station there."},{"startMs":64000,"endMs":67001,"text":"And they will probably have some traffic problems there. I want you to be there."},{"startMs":69001,"endMs":74000,"text":"At a meeting of all station personnel, volunteer workers were thoroughly brief."},{"startMs":75001,"endMs":84001,"text":"As he mentioned, we do have we have five teams here. So for the Friday's team, team number one, the team captain is Mr. Charles"},{"startMs":84001,"endMs":97001,"text":"Munn. He will be located. His team first will consist of himself, Dr. Reagan, two nurses from St. Francis Hospital,"},{"startMs":98000,"endMs":104000,"text":"and two volunteers. Now we can't..."},{"startMs":104000,"endMs":115001,"text":"We would like team number one to come up to the table here where we have the equipment displayed and actually set up a station as they will tomorrow. And we"},{"startMs":115001,"endMs":120000,"text":"would like to ask that all the people in the room volunteer to have a shot."},{"startMs":121001,"endMs":128000,"text":"And now that he's finished, will you come around this way and get your pardon please."},{"startMs":134000,"endMs":137001,"text":"Let's make Columbus the best vaccinated city in America."},{"startMs":137001,"endMs":139000,"text":"Children, bring your parents."},{"startMs":140001,"endMs":146001,"text":"Get your free polio shot today at Hershey's store."},{"startMs":148000,"endMs":150001,"text":"Join the march to health at Hershey's store."},{"startMs":152000,"endMs":155000,"text":"Get your free polio shot today at Hershey's store."},{"startMs":157000,"endMs":159001,"text":"A simple injection means polio protection."},{"startMs":160001,"endMs":164000,"text":"Let's make Columbus the best vaccinated city in America."},{"startMs":165001,"endMs":169000,"text":"Children, bring your parents. And parents, bring your children."},{"startMs":170000,"endMs":170001,"text":"Hershey's store."},{"startMs":172001,"endMs":181000,"text":"Ten days after the program was first announced, television and newsmen gathered to record the grand opening of the polio station on the main street of the city."},{"startMs":183000,"endMs":185000,"text":"The mayor was there."},{"startMs":187001,"endMs":190001,"text":"He got the first shot."},{"startMs":203000,"endMs":206001,"text":"And then another for the benefit of photographers."},{"startMs":208001,"endMs":213001,"text":"Nursing schools use the campaign as a practical training ground for student nurses."},{"startMs":217000,"endMs":221001,"text":"The mayor remained to see the community effort well on its way."},{"startMs":224000,"endMs":228001,"text":"It was an extremely pleasant start, a good omen for the campaign."},{"startMs":229000,"endMs":232000,"text":"Let's make Columbus the best vaccinated city in America."},{"startMs":234000,"endMs":237001,"text":"Children, bring your parents. And parents, bring your children."},{"startMs":239000,"endMs":242001,"text":"Get your free polio shot today at 12th and Broadway."},{"startMs":242001,"endMs":249000,"text":"Doc pulls gun on cop. Good publicity depends on taking advantage of unusual situations."},{"startMs":249001,"endMs":251000,"text":"This action made the front pages."},{"startMs":257000,"endMs":264001,"text":"Civic clubs had immunization parties. They came in groups to get their shots."},{"startMs":275001,"endMs":278001,"text":"The J sets had a big following."},{"startMs":285000,"endMs":291001,"text":"Mobile stations were set up in selected locations in other sections of the city."},{"startMs":292001,"endMs":294001,"text":"These locations were changed each day."},{"startMs":303000,"endMs":306001,"text":"Card tables and bowling chairs were readily portable."},{"startMs":309000,"endMs":312000,"text":"And the station was in operation almost immediately."},{"startMs":350000,"endMs":354001,"text":"Mobile station number two was located at a large shopping center."},{"startMs":374000,"endMs":379000,"text":"Station number three was set up at a busy street intersection in a crowded neighborhood."},{"startMs":403001,"endMs":408001,"text":"A popular grocery store served as the background for mobile station number four."},{"startMs":417001,"endMs":420000,"text":"Every shot won a balloon."},{"startMs":433001,"endMs":440001,"text":"In another section of the city, a food store in a shopping center helped to attract people to mobile station number five."},{"startMs":452000,"endMs":456001,"text":"The mobile stations were moved to new locations each day."},{"startMs":457000,"endMs":460000,"text":"This was station number two on the second day of the campaign."},{"startMs":465001,"endMs":476001,"text":"Small industries and large factories"},{"startMs":476001,"endMs":478001,"text":"were a scheduled part of the program."},{"startMs":484001,"endMs":494001,"text":"Special events were handled by a roving immunization station, which could respond quickly to any special situation, as in the case of these contestants in the Miss"},{"startMs":494001,"endMs":497001,"text":"Columbus beauty pageant, who helped to publicize the program."},{"startMs":533001,"endMs":543000,"text":"At the completion of the campaign's initial phase, exactly eight days and 38 locations later, one quarter of the city's population had received either their"},{"startMs":543000,"endMs":553000,"text":"first, second, or third shot. Although Columbus was a relatively well-immunized city at the start of the campaign, it is apparent that this phase was"},{"startMs":553000,"endMs":554001,"text":"successful beyond anticipation."},{"startMs":555001,"endMs":561000,"text":"The program will continue in two additional immunization efforts each three weeks apart."},{"startMs":561000,"endMs":572001,"text":"The final answer will be determined by a statistical study, which can then be related to the original survey. Meanwhile, new protection from polio has been"},{"startMs":572001,"endMs":577001,"text":"assured to the previously unprotected babies and breadwinners of Columbus, Georgia."},{"startMs":594001,"endMs":595001,"text":"Thank you."}]}